{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what","id":505565,"title":"The Pure defeat the Forsaken - and then what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-06T08:28:20-07:00","id":505565,"title":"The Pure defeat the Forsaken - and then what?","content":"The following assumption: The Pure defeat the Forsaken and most Uratha are now Pure. And then what? The conflict defines the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:31:15-07:00","id":505590,"title":"","content":"Some think without the Forsaken, Pangaea will return. <br /> <br /> Either way, the Forsaken will no longer be there to stop them from bringing back the old or creating a new Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:40:05-07:00","id":505619,"title":"","content":"They try to figure out a way to tear down the Gauntlet before falling to bickering and in-fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:45:21-07:00","id":505627,"title":"","content":"And then they're fucked. The spirits will come and claim their dues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:49:25-07:00","id":505630,"title":"","content":"Could they ever really defeat the Forsaken though? It's not enough to just wipe out the existing packs since anyone, anywhere could become a Werewolf at any time. Even if they wiped out all the existing members of a tribe, that tribe's totem could induct new members (and killing a spirit like Fenris-Ur would be nigh impossible)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:20:25-07:00","id":505682,"title":"","content":"In a less serious game? Werewolf party! (Best party.)<br /> <br /> In a more serious game? They'll probably be screwed, since the Uratha fulfil some pretty important roles in the Material-Shadow &quot;ecosystem&quot;. Like dealing with Shartha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:21:04-07:00","id":505683,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if the fewer forsaken there are, the more werewolves change away from Pure influence. That's what I would do in Luna's position.<br /> <br /> Although I think the whole &quot;Pure outnumber Forsaken 2 to 1&quot; is purely an American thing. Globally I would be willing to bet Ghost Wolves outnumber everyone else by a considerable margin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:27:23-07:00","id":505687,"title":"","content":"The numbers are supposed to shift in cycles. We're just at an optimum time for Pure antagonism.<br /> <br /> Essentially once the Forsaken get too numerous, they push the Pure to the far reaches, then turn to in-fighting. That's what the Brethren War was. The Pure then take advantage of this, waiting for the optimum moment to strike and do so, destroying key Forsaken and overturning territories and so forth. They convert more and more until they get all fat and overconfident as the Forsaken slowly rise in numbers and strike back against them when they hear a call for their duty and know the Pure are standing in their way.<br /> <br /> In times and places of trouble, the Pure numbers dwindle. During periods of complacency, the Pure rule.<br /> <br /> Right now we're a bit well past the Brethren War, at least in first edition, and the Pure are ascendant, but rumors of idigam are rising, and times of trouble are coming and the Forsaken are or were being called to do their duty. And the Pure are in their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-06-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:37:41-07:00","id":505700,"title":"","content":"While there hasn't been a whole lot of info on the Pure yet in the new edition, what little there has been makes me think that not too much would change for the pure. The Preditor Kings would continue to be obsessed with hunting and killing those who disrespect the hunt. This would probably mean they'd kill a lot more humans who think they're big-shots or vampires who have gotten lazy with easy access to blood. Fire-Touched would still be crazy street-preachers who hunt down Mages and mortal mediums (and maybe Shartha) that disrespect the Shadow. Ivory Claws would continue to track the lineages of the various supernatural taints they know of in the greater human populace, killing anyone that disrespects or defiles their heritage or otherwise gets on the Ivory-Claws' nerves.<br /> While the Forsaken fall under the umbrella of each Pure Tribe's sacred prey, all three spread wider than the Forsaken. Even without the Forsaken, the Pure have plenty to keep their crazy selves occupied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:40:23-07:00","id":505706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505700#post505700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Preditor Kings would continue to be obsessed with hunting and killing those who disrespect the hunt. This would probably mean they'd kill a lot more humans who think they're big-shots or vampires who have gotten lazy with easy access to blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, I hadn't thought of that. Hopefully we'll get a Predator Kings pack with a strix totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T09:51:37-07:00","id":505723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then what? The conflict defines the Pure. </div> </div> </div>Go after Luna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:04:26-07:00","id":505730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505706#post505706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully we'll get a Predator Kings pack with a strix totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with that is the Strix aren't spirits. They are ephemeral beings, but they don't come from the Shadow and can't be appeased the same way spirits can. It would be like having a ghost or an Angel as a totem. A Strix would probably laugh at the Predator Kings trying to petition it as a totem before attempting to possess one of their bodies.<br /> <br /> However that doesn't mean they couldn't form an alliance to hunt vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:07:05-07:00","id":505731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505730#post505730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with that is the Strix aren't spirits. They are ephemeral beings, but they don't come from the Shadow and can't be appeased the same way spirits can. It would be like having a ghost or an Angel as a totem. A Strix would probably laugh at the Predator Kings trying to petition it as a totem before attempting to possess one of their bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, we all know the rules. But Synthesis does allow for an exception, and rule of cool always trumps, 'No it can't happen.' Especially with the Fourth Commandment being, 'Don't Say No.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:13:14-07:00","id":505739,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure a strix could possess a spirit. <br /> <br /> It may well go along with a werewolf pack for shits and giggles though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:18:38-07:00","id":505743,"title":"","content":"As far as things with the Pure would go if they defeated the Forsaken and took over: Chaos.<br /> <br /> Their attempt to remake Pangaea would cause spirits to run rampant. Their superior attitudes and notions of &quot;Fuck Prey&quot; would lead them into open conflict with humans and supernaturals. Plus the Idigam running around would cause a lot of problems for them. They might run into conflict with Luna and her Lunes too, depending on how pissed she was about her children being slain. And then there would be infighting, and perhaps dissident, as younger werewolves start seeing flaws in their tribes' dogmas. Many might forge out on their own, becoming Ghost Wolves or looking to start a new tribe. Essentially, in the end the Pure would be reduced to filling the niche the Forsaken left behind, becoming more like their enemy then they would like.<br /> <br /> Human society would probably go down the toilet as well because the spirit world wouldn't be in balance. Violence, possessions, and spirit worship would rise. And then the Bale Hounds and their Maeljin masters would not be far behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","user":"Nuwisha Nutjob","date":". 05-06-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:55:52-07:00","id":505915,"title":"","content":"You can't defeat the concept of freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T12:01:23-07:00","id":505922,"title":"","content":"As above, but also:<br /> <br /> Internal Factionalism. The Pure are barely united as-is. Remove the external threat/unifying racial enemy of the Forsaken, you're likely to run into dissension and eventual bloodshed.<br /> <br /> New External Threats. Without their traditional enemies the Pure are going to greatly expand their areas of influence... and start pissing off other power factions. A cabal of Awakened might take a dim very of trying to destroy the Gauntlet, vampires will act to protect their own hunting grounds. With enough poor decision-making the Pure might push groups like Task Force: Valkyrie (among others) to the nuclear option of going public... and using the funding to mass produce anti-werewolf weaponry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T12:37:00-07:00","id":505971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505630#post505630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could they ever really defeat the Forsaken though?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Every first change away from them will have an auspice. The Pure would need to kill Luna the way the Forsaken killed Urfarah in order to defeat them, and that event would prove as much apocalyptic as the first instance of patricide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:35:23-07:00","id":506411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505971#post505971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Every first change away from them will have an auspice. The Pure would need to kill Luna the way the Forsaken killed Urfarah in order to defeat them, and that event would prove as much apocalyptic as the first instance of patricide.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually quite simple.<br /> <br /> We kill the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:41:51-07:00","id":506415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=505915#post505915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't defeat the concept of freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not what the Forsaken are though. They have a distinct culture based around their duty to the Hunt and the Oaths of the Moon. Cultural traditions and identities can be destroyed. At very least it's conceivable that a world could exist where the Uratha are divided between the Pure and Auspiced Ghost-Wolves, who cling to their freedom hiding from the Pure who hunt them, without a uniting cultural heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-07-2015, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:53:56-07:00","id":506418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=506411#post506411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We kill the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible someone or something is already planning it. P173, Tribes of the Moon, 'One woman's visions gave birth to the Lodge of the Final Winter. She saw the moon broken from its orbit and pulled toward Gaea by a great evil within the Shadow, and great gray-white shards of lunar rock rained upon the world as the Mother disintegrated in the heavens.' There's a two page 'sidebar' afterwards offering advice on how to run it.<br /> <br /> With Luna gone, all you have to do is take out the Forsaken totems, though they would all probably get tremendous boosts in power as such an event would cause a lot of effects they resonate with. Death, darkness, destruction, change and winter. At least I think that's them. Just getting rid of Luna and 'freeing' the Forsaken might be enough for a lot of Pure.<br /> <br /> Man, it's such a fun setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:42:07-07:00","id":506710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/505565-the-pure-defeat-the-forsaken-and-then-what?p=506411#post506411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually quite simple.<br /> <br /> We kill the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did not mean Hitler?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-b